# Loop chords only at the top

When a song uses the **same chord progression throughout** (e.g. 3–5 chords in a repeating loop):

1. Put the chords **once** at the top in a `\beginverse*` / `{\nolyrics …}` jam-chart line
2. Mark it clearly with **`(Loop)`**
3. **Do not** place `\[…]` chords inside verses or choruses
4. Lyrics stay chord-free so they stay readable and fit one page better

```tex
% ✅ GOOD
\beginverse*
{\nolyrics Jam chart: \[Em] \[G] \[Bm] \[Bm] \quad (Loop)}
\endverse

\beginverse
I fell in love with impossible \brk  Shook hands with a man named intangible
\endverse

% ❌ BAD — same loop repeated above random words
\beginverse
I fell in love with im\[Em]possible \brk  Shook hands with a man named in\[G]tangible
\endverse
```

Only keep inline chords when the progression **changes by section** (different verse/chorus/bridge charts).
